&lt;p&gt;# Comments: 0&lt;/p&gt;</description><guid isPermaLink="false">https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=49842514</guid><pubDate>Fri, 25 Sep 2026 10:23:41 +0000</pubDate></item><item><title>Tell HN: PSA: AI can make old games run on 64-bit macOS</title><link>https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=49842482</link><description>&lt;p&gt;I had Aviary Attorney lying around (great game, whether or not you like Phoenix Wright) but it wouldn't run on newer macOS versions.&lt;p&gt;I tried asking Astra on a whim, looked away, and within a few minutes it was on screen!&lt;p&gt;Turns out "The game used 32-bit Node-WebKit, an old combination of Node.js and Chromium that modern macOS cannot run. Its actual game content was HTML, JavaScript, images, and audio, so replacing the runtime was feasible."&lt;p&gt;Guess I got lucky in this case.&lt;/p&gt;
